# Python standards
- Python 3.13; type hints for public functions; pathlib and dataclasses where appropriate.
- Prefer small, pure functions and dependency injection over global mutable state.
- Use subprocess.run with argument arrays, shell=False, check=True, timeouts, explicit cwd or git -C. Never interpolate untrusted input into a shell.
- Handle Git output as bytes when dealing with filenames; use -z for name/status output and decode using surrogateescape where appropriate.
- Use -- before Git pathspecs. Validate revision parameters and avoid option injection; resolve revisions to commit object IDs before diffing.
- Read tracked content from the selected Git commit (git show <sha>:<path> or cat-file), not the worktree.
- Handle malformed UTF-8, SyntaxError, missing objects, subprocess errors, timeout, and paths with spaces/unicode.
- Avoid quadratic scanning when indexing imports. Build module-name lookup and reverse-import index in one pass, with clear complexity bounds.
- Distinguish confirmed references from heuristic candidates.
- Add unittest tests for normal and edge cases, and temporary local Git repositories for integration tests.
